Summary: Agent-Centric Architecture
Core Concept
Agents are the primary abstraction, not workflows. Each agent:

Contains its own workflow (6-12 steps max)
Can call other agents (which have their own workflows)
Handles its own error boundaries
Manages its own state decisions

Architecture Pattern
Agent A (with workflow)
  → calls → Agent B (with workflow)
              → calls → Agent C (with workflow)
              → returns to B
  → returns to A

Key Implementation Changes
1. Agent as First-Class Citizen

type Agent struct {
    ID          string
    Type        string
    Workflow    WorkflowPlan      // Embedded, not referenced
    ErrorPolicy ErrorHandlingPolicy
    StateConfig StateConfiguration
}

2. Workflow Steps Call Agents, Not Actions
# Current (action-based)
step:
  action: "transform_data"
  topic: "some.topic"

# New (agent-based)
step:
  action: "call_agent"
  agent_type: "data_transformer"
  agent_id: "optional_specific_instance"

3. Agent Registry/Discovery
type AgentRegistry struct {
    // Find agents by capability
    FindAgent(agentType string, capabilities []string) (Agent, error)
    // Register agent availability
    RegisterAgent(agent Agent) error
}

