The (Weak) Case for Optional
1. "Load Balancing"
# The argument: "Let Kafka/system choose any available instance"
step:
  agent_type: "analyzer"
  # No ID specified, any analyzer can handle it

Counter: Load balancing should happen at infrastructure level, not workflow level. The orchestrator should resolve to a specific instance.
2. "Simplicity"
Counter: It's not simpler - it's ambiguous. Debugging "some analyzer somewhere failed" is much harder than "analyzer-prod-v3-instance-2 failed".
Why Mandatory Wins
1. Deterministic Execution
// At orchestration time, resolve to specific instance
func (s *SagaCoordinator) resolveAgent(agentType string) (AgentInstance, error) {
    // Even if using "round-robin" or "least-loaded"
    // We resolve to a SPECIFIC instance
    instance := s.loadBalancer.SelectInstance(agentType)

    // Record this decision
    s.recordAgentSelection(correlationID, stepName, instance.ID)

    return instance, nil
}

