Improved Design
type Step struct {
    Action      string

    // For agent calls - BOTH mandatory
    AgentType   string  // "analyzer"
    AgentID     string  // "analyzer-prod-v3-instance-1"

    // How to select if not specified in workflow
    SelectionStrategy string // "latest", "stable", "canary", "specific"
}

type AgentSelector struct {
    // Called during workflow execution
    SelectAgent(agentType string, strategy string) (AgentInstance, error)
}

// Workflow can specify selection strategy
step:
  action: call_agent
  agent_type: analyzer
  selection_strategy: stable  # Orchestrator picks specific stable instance

# Or explicit instance (for debugging/testing)
step:
  action: call_agent
  agent_type: analyzer
  agent_id: analyzer-test-v4-debug-1

The Hybrid Approach (Best of Both)
type Step struct {
    Action       string
    AgentType    string

    // ONE of these must be set:
    AgentID      string // Explicit instance
    AgentSelector string // Selection strategy: "latest", "stable", "canary"
}

// At execution time:
func (s *SagaCoordinator) executeAgentCall(step Step) error {
    var agentID string

    if step.AgentID != "" {
        agentID = step.AgentID
    } else {
        // Resolve to specific instance using selector
        instance, err := s.agentRegistry.Select(step.AgentType, step.AgentSelector)
        if err != nil {
            return err
        }
        agentID = instance.ID
    }

    // ALWAYS log the specific instance used
    s.recordExecution(ExecutionRecord{
        Step:     step.Name,
        AgentID:  agentID,  // ALWAYS recorded
        Timestamp: time.Now(),
    })
}

Conclusion
You're right - AgentID should not be optional at execution time. Even if the workflow doesn't specify a particular instance, the orchestrator should:

Resolve to a specific instance
Record that decision
Execute with that specific instance

This gives you:

Complete observability
Reliable debugging
Version tracking
Graph integrity
Audit compliance

The workflow can express "I don't care which analyzer" via selection strategy, but the execution MUST record "analyzer-prod-v3-instance-2 was used".

